nd of  movement so the hunger for a discussion  of ideas v I mean they do often have  some legitimate complaints about some  ridiculous things the left does some  excesses of you know cultural  appropriation analysis or what-have-you  and if you if you moderate those  tendencies and you you make it so that  you are able to appeal to the people  they might capture I think you can peel  a lot of them off I I mean what I  advocate always I mean I say this over  and over I'm a broken record is building  an alternative  you can't just denounce them but if you  build an alternative that people see as  reasonable then you can you can sort of  neutralize them I'll a talk about that I  want it I want to hear about what would  that alternative look like but in a very  specific way I want to couch that  question because the intellectual  darkweb claims to have significant  political diversity right they say we  are not here because we are liberal or  liberal or conservative you have  right-wingers that that are involved  like ben shapiro do you have sort of the  ambivalent center right I guess  classical liberal maybe is what they  like to call themselves I call it the  ambivalent Center right you have  supposed liberals like brett weinstein i  don't know if eric also considers  himself a liberal maybe he does so they  claim that it's not actually about their  placement on the political spectrum but  that it's about something else so given  that how do you build a successful sort  of alternative to it um well what you  really want i mean i look again you have  to pick who you're trying to persuade i  think there are i think that's probably  true i mean i get emails from people you  know every time i read an article about  one of these guys who say well I  consider myself on the left but I like  these guys because I think they tell it  like it is yeah and I'm not gonna wear  the left is never going to appeal to the  hardcore Shapiro's types but I mean I  think he is like I don'